---
// The counters of one proposal. Props only, and no program data of any kind: the
// figures below say how a scale was answered, never by whom or for which
// formation.
//
// The block is rendered whole at build and never hidden. What a build cannot know
// is the figures alone, so the labels, the qualification and the five rows are
// here from the start and only the value cells wait. Three consequences, all
// intended: the slot has a stable size, so the page does not jump when the
// counters arrive (System §5.9); a reader without JavaScript sees the section
// state that its figures are pending rather than see nothing; and no failure can
// make the section disappear, because nothing removes it (INV-14, P8).
//
// The five modalities are in scale order, each with its full formulation. No data
// mark is drawn: a bar would add nothing to the figure beside it, and under the
// threshold it would restate in a length the precision the threshold exists to
// withhold. Nothing here is a value scale and nothing carries a tint (INV-12,
// DP-22, G5).
//
// `state` is the one line that changes: it holds the count, or the reason there
// is none. The qualification below it does not change — an aggregate is a
// self-selected sample whatever its size (DP-15).
const { question, labels, title, pending, sample } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="aggregate" data-question={question}>
  <p class="aggregate-title"><strong>{title}</strong></p>
  <p class="aggregate-state">{pending}</p>
  <ul class="aggregate-rows">
    {
      labels.map((label, choice) => (
        <li>
          <span>{label}</span>
          <span class="aggregate-value" data-choice={choice} />
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ul>
  <p class="aggregate-sample">{sample}</p>
</div>
